matmul.cpp, 2026-11-24

Multi-row B reuse experiment (matmul_multirow)

Apple Clang 17.0.0 on arm64, compiled with -std=c++17 -O3.
One row uses the existing untiled reordered kernel. Row counts 2, 4,
8, and 16 use the same template with fixed row counts and sequential
column iteration. Each configuration had one warm-up, then five timed
runs at 1024 and 2048 or three at 4096. Trial order alternated forward
and reverse. The trials used the same seeded FP32 inputs and included
output allocation and initialization. Correctness checks were untimed.

The 4096 finalists were selected by geometric mean of speedups at
1024 and 2048. Active C is the storage spanned by the output rows
being updated. It is calculated as rows × columns × 4 bytes.
GFLOP/s uses 2 × M × K × N divided by the mean runtime.

The 1024 reference used naive multiplication. The 2048 and 4096
references used reordered multiplication and were independently
checked at nine positions using double-precision dot products.

